        "text": "Page: Rensselaer Plateau. Sentence: Vegetation on the plateau is more similar to that found in the Adirondack Mountains to the northwest, with abundant Eastern White Pine, Eastern Hemlock, Red Spruce, and Balsam Fir, along with more limited occurrences of Red Pine and Tamarack.\nPage: Picea rubens. Sentence: Picea rubens, commonly known as red spruce, is a species of spruce native to eastern North America, ranging from eastern Quebec to Nova Scotia, and from New England south in the Adirondack Mountains and Appalachians to western North Carolina.\nPage: Round Pond (Berlin, New York). Sentence: The lake is located on a geologic formation known as the Rensselaer Plateau.",
